Z||000000||MontanaFiero||03-06-2001||10:19 PM||||Still toying with putting the '93 3.4Litre Camaro motor in my '86 SE (well waiting for Rapid Refund, actually). I'm  considering using the camaro system, manifold, DIS, computer, etc. Combining the wiring harnesses is cake for me, but my concern is for the Thermostat housing. Anyone done this? and did the housing clear the camaro manifold? <BR>While we're on the subject, anything else I am overlooking (I know about the starter relocation)<P>------------------<BR>&gt;&gt; '87 Coupe 4 cyl, auto &lt;&lt;<BR>&gt;&gt; '86 SE V6, 4 speed- <I>project</I> &lt;&lt;||||reg||5
Z||000001||Black88GT||03-06-2001||10:41 PM||||If you are going to go through all of that trouble you might as well go with a newer 3.4 with better heads and intake.<P>------------------<BR>Jeff<BR>'88 GT t-top 3.4<BR>Baltimore, MD<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.geocities.com/fieropage/af.bmp"> ||||reg||1
Z||000002||Cooter||03-06-2001||10:47 PM||||Yep- the new FWD 3.4's have great flowing aluminum heads and a roller cam. If you are going to be wiring for DIS, go ahead and get the FWD engine.||||reg||1
