Z||000005||Will||03-07-2001||12:16 AM|||| <A HREF="http://www.gmpowertrain.com/engines_cartruck/other/34_main.htm" TARGET=_blank>http://www.gmpowertrain.com/engines_cartruck/other/34_main.htm</A> <BR>lists the applications for the LA1 3.4L V6 as: base engine in: Monte carlo, Impala; optional in Grand Am, Alero. That is for the 2000 model year, I think. I don't know how long the engine has been used in those cars. It has also been (and is currently?) used in minvans and is currently used in the A$$tek (rip the engine out of the first one you see parked anywhere--on less of them on the road)<BR> I've been waiting for someone to come up with the balls and common sense to do this swap! I'd do it, but I have another underway.<BR>The conventional swap--taking an engine with DIS and going back to a distributor system--never made sense to me.<BR>If your good with wiring, go for it! Too many people are deathly afraid of this very simple aspect of swapping engines. I don't get it.||||reg||1
